  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Transitive ichidan verb. Xを{貯|た}める. The intransitive pair is {貯|た}まる (to accumulate).\n\nWritten with {貯|た} specifically for saving money or points. The homophone {溜|た}める covers accumulating things in general — water, stress, unfinished work.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- お{金|かね}を{貯|た}める: to save money\n- {貯金|ちょきん}を{貯|た}める: to build up savings\n- ポイントを{貯|た}める: to collect points\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {貯金|ちょきん}する: to save money — noun + する; emphasizes the act of depositing\n- {溜|た}める: to accumulate — general accumulation, not specifically money",
